    FLARE-3096: Downgrade harmless abort and fail logs to INFO (#5051)
    
    ## Summary
    
    When a late stop, abort, or failure report reaches a job that has
    already left `JobRunner.running_jobs`, the condition is an expected
    lifecycle race rather than a server error. This change downgrades those
    messages from ERROR to INFO while preserving the returned status message
    for callers.
    
    The fix intentionally leaves `ServerEngine.run_processes` cleanup with
    the existing asynchronous launcher cleanup path instead of mutating
    process maps from the job-start exception handler.
    
    Jira: [FLARE-3096](https://jirasw.nvidia.com/browse/FLARE-3096)
    NVBug: 6563308
    
    ## Validation
    
    - `58 passed`: `job_runner_test.py` and `fed_server_test.py`
    - Scoped `./runtest.sh -s` passed for both changed files
    - Added coverage for late abort, late failure, and `stop_all_runs()`
    encountering an untracked process
    
    Co-authored-by: Yuan-Ting Hsieh (謝沅廷) <yuantingh@nvidia.com>
